WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
- Most of you are not
doing what you want to do

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.320
with your life
because you're worried

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.120
about someone else's opinion.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.800
Normally,
your fucked up mom,

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.440
or your spouse,

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.000
or somebody very close to
you is fucking your shit up.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.280
(audience laughter)

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.360
Right, so that's awesome
for me, but on the flip side

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.360
in the macro of
me not giving a shit

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.880
when somebody leaves one comment
on an Instagram post like,

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.320
this guy is a scam artist.
I'm like strategizing

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:29.320
how to fix that like
it's the most important thing

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.400
that has ever happened to me.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.080
Pulling from opposite directions

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.200
is like a bridge, my friends.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.280
It is not something
that you should be scared of.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:41.280
Way too many people
think it's a contradiction,

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.280
think it's a flaw.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.200
When you define what
true intelligence is,

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.600
it is holding
opposite things in your head

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.120
and allowing them to push.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:53.040
I love that
everything is easy to me.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.400
We were having fun
beforehand, I'm like,

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.760
what's this thing I'm
doing after my keynote,

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.200
and they're laughing, they're
like, you didn't read it?

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.480
I'm like, I haven't
read shit in 20 years.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:04.760
I don't need to be
prepared, I stay in my lane.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.560
The reason I love doing
Q&amp;amp;A is if I don't know

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.880
the answer to
your question I'll say

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:09.840
I don't know the
answer to your question.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.840
We are fronting, we are
fronting in our society.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.640
You need to triple down,
quadruple down on who you are

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.880
and what you know,
and then you can win.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.120
When people ask me
how do I produce content?

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:24.120
One big breakthrough in
my community was when about

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.560
six months ago I said, you
know what, you should document

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.119
instead of create.

00:01:29.119 --> 00:01:31.919
It opened up so much for
so many when they realized,

00:01:31.919 --> 00:01:35.720
wait a minute, right,
you need to be documenting

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:39.200
in your stories or in
your vlog about the journey

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.360
of becoming an entrepreneur,
not claiming that you're

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:47.440
a 21-year-old life coach,
and pay me $5,000 a month

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.820
and I'll teach you how
to fucking live, fuck you.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.820
(light music)

